    hindiMeaning: "ये सभी (चारों प्रकार के भक्त) निश्चय ही उदार (महान) हैं; परंतु ज्ञानी तो साक्षात् मेरी अपनी ही आत्मा है—ऐसा मेरा मत है! क्योंकि वह एकाग्रचित्त होकर मुझको ही अपनी सर्वोच्च (परम) गति मानकर मुझमें ही भलीभांति स्थित है। यह भगवान श्री कृष्ण के हृदय की अगाध करुणा और भक्त-वात्सल्य का शिखर है: 1. 'उदाराः सर्व एवैते': भगवान कितने दयालु हैं! जो केवल संकट में या धन के लिए आए, भगवान ने उन्हें दुत्कारा नहीं बल्कि 'उदार' (महान) कहा, क्योंकि वे कम से कम संसार के आगे हाथ फैलाने के बजाय प्रभु के पास आए। 2. 'ज्ञानी त्वात्मैव मे मतम्': किंतु ज्ञानी भक्त के लिए भगवान कहते हैं—'ज्ञानी तो साक्षात् मेरी अपनी आत्मा है!' (Jnani is My very Self). 3. 'मामेवानुत्तमां गतिम्': ज्ञानी भक्त के जीवन का एक ही ध्येय, एक ही विश्राम और एक ही गंतव्य है—स्वयं भगवान श्रीकृष्ण!",
    englishMeaning: "Noble indeed are all these seekers; but the person of wisdom (Jnani) I consider to be My very Self! For with mind steadily absorbed, they are established in Me alone as the supreme and unexcelled destination! Sri Krishna displays His magnificent divine magnanimity and unveils the ultimate intimacy between God and the enlightened soul: 1. Cosmic Generosity towards All Seekers (Udarah sarva evaite): The Lord does not belittle those who seek relief from sorrow or ask for material blessings. He honors them as noble (Udarah), because instead of chasing corrupt paths, they chose to seek shelter in the Divine. 2. Jnani tv Atmaiva Me Matam (The Wise Seeker is My Very Self): While all seekers are beloved, Sri Krishna makes an astounding declaration about the Jnani: 'The wise soul is not merely a worshiper—they are My very Self (Atmaiva)!' 3. Mam Evanuttamam Gatim: Because the Jnani's consciousness has identified Sri Krishna as the singular, supreme goal, the Lord reciprocates by dwelling fully within the Jnani's heart.",
    lifeLesson: "Do not judge others harshly for where they are on their spiritual or personal journey. Everyone who turns toward goodness and honesty—even for basic comfort or support—is worthy of respect. At the same time, make your ultimate goal self-realization and pure love. When you seek truth for its own sake, you realize that the Divine is not an external figure to be bribed with favors, but the very soul and center of your own being."
